  data:  # d1db
    kind: work_item  # d1db
    title: "metrics.avg_confidence=0.8 hides 6-spike multimodal distribution"  # d1db
    status: todo_hard  # d1db
    priority: 2  # d1db
    parent:  # d1db
    tags:  # d1db
    - dogfood_tranch_03  # d1db
    - dogfood  # d1db
    isbefore: []  # d1db
    duplicate_of: []  # d1db
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d1db
    pr_ref:  # d1db
    description: "**Mechanic**: The top-level scalar `avg_confidence` summarizes 110,533 edges as a single decimal. The underlying distribution has six tight spikes at 0.85 (41,730), 0.95 (19,295), 1.0 (18,388), 0.4 (16,331), 0.5 (7,928), 0.9 (4,741). Only 62 edges hit the spec MATRIX default of 0.30 (all of type `type_hierarchy`). Each spike is a per-evidence-type hardcoded value rather than a continuous distribution.\n\n**Expectation**: The reported summary statistic reflects the distribution shape — either an additional histogram field, a mode/median, or a multimodal flag — so a consumer is not misled into treating a 6-spike distribution as smooth.\n\n**Scope**: Top-level `metrics.avg_confidence` on every substrate; six spikes account for ~99% of edges.\n\n**Exposure**: Any dashboard reporting \"this analysis has avg confidence 0.8\"; any consumer doing `confidence > avg_confidence` slicing.\n\n**Consequence**: Dashboards imply a centered distribution; in reality slicing on `avg_confidence` cuts at one of the spike values and produces nondeterministic-feeling thresholds.\n\n**Source**: F49.A4 (INDEPENDENT, HIGH).\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # d1db
    fields: {}  # d1db
- op: discuss  # 46d1
